# The object that `choose` makes is never built: the call returns a tag and the reference that the object would hold. Where the tag says null, that second word is whatever the register held.
# IR: function f2 name="weigh"
# IR: v{{*}}: unspecified|L0 @Cell = ResultAt v{{*}} index=1
# So the back end is told nothing of it, and its read stays behind the test of the tag. It is told of the parameter, which is always an object.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="weigh" role=Source
# CHECK: Int32, Int64 b@[[results]] = Patchpoint(b@[[entry]]:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[tag]] = Extract(b@[[results]], <<0, 
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[chosen]] = Extract(b@[[results]], <<1, 
# CHECK-NOT: b@[[chosen]]
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[isChosen]], Else:#
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[isChosen]]:
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[chosen]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: Known properties:
# CHECK-NEXT: b@[[entry]]: dereferenceableBytes = 32
# CHECK-NOT: dereferenceableBytes
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
